{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.threeCalibrationDiscipline_mass_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.threeCalibrationDiscipline_mass_pos","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L157-L173","doc":"**Positivity consequence of the discipline** — *derived*, not assumed:\na mass with a positive realised tower value is itself positive.\n\nComposes the factorisation with the two calibration-scale positivity\nhypotheses `m_e_pos`, `m_pi_pos` (the `q_0` modulus enters only through\n`towerValue`, whose positivity is the antecedent). The conclusion\n`0 < mass X` appears in no class field — this is the discipline earning\na real inference: the two dimensional scales `m_e`, `m_π` never flip a\npositive dimensionless tower amplitude to a non-positive mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.threeCalibrationDiscipline","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.threeCalibrationDiscipline","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L135-L155","doc":"Headline statement ([`def:three-calibration-discipline`]): under\n`ThreeCalibrationDiscipline`, every mass factors as\n`m_e^a · m_π^c · Q_ℝ(q_0)` where `Q_ℝ(q_0)` is the realised real value\n(`towerValue`) of the dimensionless `ℚ[q^{±1}]`-tower at the substrate\nparameter.\n\nThis faithfully surfaces the discipline *axiom* — the factorisation is\na structural assumption on how the algebraic-side chain realises the\nmass functional (AGENTS.md §3b), not a result derived from more\nprimitive Lean data; its content lives in the class field\n`mass_factorisation`. The genuinely-derived consequence that exercises\nthe discipline (and its scale-positivity hypotheses) is\n`threeCalibrationDiscipline_mass_pos` below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:three-calibration-discipline","label":"def:three-calibration-discipline","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.mass_factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.mass_factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L128-L128","doc":"The discipline:\n`mass X = m_e^{a(X)} · m_π^{c(X)} · towerValue(X)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.mass","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The mass functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_pi_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_pi_degree","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_e_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_e_degree","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L122-L122","doc":"Cohomological-grading exponents supplied by the observable:\n`a` counts `m_e` insertions, `c` counts meson-sector (`m_π`)\ninsertions (`c = 0` for the baryon sector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.towerValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.towerValue","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L118-L118","doc":"The realised dimensionless tower value `Q_X(q_0) ∈ ℝ`, obtained\nby casting a `ℚ[q^{±1}]`-element along `ℚ → ℝ` and evaluating at\n`q_0`. The algebraic-side framework constructs every tower\nelement strictly inside `ℚ[q^{±1}]` (Wedderburn weights ×\nMarkov-trace polynomials in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`); the cast to `ℝ` is the\nfinal archimedean step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_pi_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_pi_pos","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L111-L111","doc":"Positivity of the meson scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_pi","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L109-L109","doc":"CAL-3: meson-sector scale (representative `m_π`), the scale of\nthe `Vol(Hopf)=0` orthogonal class, in the same energy units as\n`m_e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.q_0_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.q_0_pos","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L105-L105","doc":"`q_0 > 1` (positivity / non-degenerate substrate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.q_0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.q_0","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L103-L103","doc":"CAL-2: dimensionless substrate parameter (the modulus of the\n`W`-Hodge plane), fixed by the lepton mass ratio `m_μ / m_e`\n(Physical-Observations may numerically anchor on `m_p / m_e`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_e_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_e_pos","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L99-L99","doc":"Positivity of the mass scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.m_e","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L97-L97","doc":"CAL-1: dimensional unit (CODATA `m_e`), the scale of the\n`W`-Hodge plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.ThreeCalibrationDiscipline","kind":"class","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L71-L133","doc":"The three-calibration discipline class.\n\nAn instance asserts that the mass functional `mass` factors as\n`m_e^a · m_π^c · towerValue(X)` for the realised tower value at\n`q_0` and non-negative integer grading exponents `a, c` supplied\nby the observable.\n\nThe three calibration inputs (`m_e`, `q_0`, `m_π`) are the three\nreal degrees of freedom of the Bring Hodge structure `H^1 = 2W`\n(`prop:calibration-cohomology-alignment`):\n\n- `m_e` is the **scale** of the rank-2 `W`-Hodge plane.\n- `q_0` is the **modulus** of that plane; the canonical CAL-2\n  observable is the neutron β-sector bar-skew channel `P_skew^β`, pinned through\n  its proxy `m_μ/m_e`.\n- `m_π` is the proxy for the **scale** of the `Vol(Hopf)=0` meson\n  sector (CAL-3 `P_avg^π`) — an orthogonal class independent of\n  `(m_e, q_0)`.\n\n`Q_β = P_skew^β (the channel’s measured energy)` is the **CAL-2 proxy**, reproduced from `m_e` and\n`q_0` as a cross-check, not an independent input. A **fourth**\ndimensional input would violate the cohomological alignment and is\na hard audit failure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HadronicState.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HadronicState.carrier","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HadronicState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HadronicState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.HadronicState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.HadronicState","kind":"structure","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/three-calibration-discipline.lean#L64-L69","doc":"A formal hadronic state — abstract carrier; the algebraic-side\nchain produces a `ℚ(q)`-valued tower expression for each such\n`X`, together with non-negative integer exponents counting the\n`m_e` and `m_π` insertions supplied by the observable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}